WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.088 --> 00:00:01.654
Open the public Moon explorer in a fresh browser.

2
00:00:01.654 --> 00:00:04.057
Drag the real 3D Moon, then locate its south pole.

3
00:00:04.057 --> 00:00:06.940
Select supported ROI 6 and enter the workspace with a real horizontal transition.

4
00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.499
Calculate and record the 24-hour darkness-limit baseline on the real cloud service.

5
00:00:10.499 --> 00:00:13.548
Tighten the darkness limit to 8 hours and compute the changed decision.

6
00:00:13.548 --> 00:00:16.038
Open the metric explanation and locate its actual continuous dark interval.

7
00:00:16.038 --> 00:00:18.581
Compare two preserved scenarios; different thresholds have no universal ranking.

8
00:00:18.581 --> 00:00:21.479
Save the complete cloud record as a named mission.

9
00:00:21.479 --> 00:00:26.904
Refresh the page and reopen the saved original from My missions; no server restart is claimed.

10
00:00:26.904 --> 00:00:28.760
Create a read-only share for a separate anonymous visitor.

11
00:00:28.852 --> 00:00:32.654
A separate browser context opens the read-only original record.

12
00:00:32.654 --> 00:00:36.320
Export complete JSON and a readable report from the same saved evidence.
